[{:db/id "q-42684/selection/30595e53f626f7114ac96a4be05b7a10ac703b6b41ea1355ccd4492abed3d444" :answer/id #uuid "230825ff-d4ff-523f-a523-da9e0ecf4ce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42684/selection/ac9ae2052cc2e067abcad4ecf5a3f3d17a02fa2d9a881931a644b74ccc7546a6" :answer/id #uuid "094ada10-82d7-5c9f-8e86-4faa7f871841" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42684/selection/40a1a273986776af283f3fe5271d8cce9b3f9fa9c2c7fc5bf8516dd5a30de4b0" :answer/id #uuid "1781ae4f-3c4c-5ca3-a32a-5b2bbf093035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42684/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae" :answer/id #uuid "3a25fc17-b3f3-5c86-a7ae-4b27e0b77a36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42684/selection/99308c630bb61642567370331cf7f00923f341daf010971193b3aeace8b32c69" :answer/id #uuid "7fcd42be-ed89-5a5c-a518-f4ed98d600a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42684/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c6457dd-d587-5b7e-a231-e7ae3d70e65b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42684/selection/30595e53f626f7114ac96a4be05b7a10ac703b6b41ea1355ccd4492abed3d444" :answer-field/choices ["q-42684/selection/30595e53f626f7114ac96a4be05b7a10ac703b6b41ea1355ccd4492abed3d444" "q-42684/selection/ac9ae2052cc2e067abcad4ecf5a3f3d17a02fa2d9a881931a644b74ccc7546a6" "q-42684/selection/40a1a273986776af283f3fe5271d8cce9b3f9fa9c2c7fc5bf8516dd5a30de4b0" "q-42684/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae" "q-42684/selection/99308c630bb61642567370331cf7f00923f341daf010971193b3aeace8b32c69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42684" :question/id #uuid "0fb3471e-ecaa-50cb-8cd9-8162fc209e2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42684" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}19x+3y-4z=-2 \\\\ 6x+ky-4z=-1 \\\\ -9x-y+2z=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that  $y=21$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $2k+20,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}19 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 6 & k & -4 \\\\ -9 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2k+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}19 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =19\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =19(-2+20)+2(12-36)-4(30-9) \\\\  & =342-48-84 \\\\  & =210.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{210}{2k+20}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=21.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{210}{2k+20} & =21 \\\\ 10 & =2k+20 \\\\ 2k & =-10 \\\\ k & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-42684/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7263e25b-117e-528c-b2ad-2624f325da35"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42684"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43108/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "df3cc546-61eb-5f4c-9996-f5e75102a637" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43108/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3d3126da-63e8-59db-9c2c-3aaa7e0ac1bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43108/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "7c7eae15-f4fc-5f73-9363-b06854255e0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43108/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "045168b7-a9c5-5cee-9654-b35d42034205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43108/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "e3b61000-5e2e-5681-a674-1729bacdbe5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43108/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a098d28-949c-5307-a661-e6105eb579fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43108/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-43108/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-43108/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-43108/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-43108/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-43108/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43108" :question/id #uuid "f798968c-00e5-5cfc-9a44-e58dbe783299" :question/math-academy-id "q-43108" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+z=1 \\\\ 5x+3y+4z=2 \\\\ x+y-z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-1,$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+1z=1 \\\\ 5x+3y+4z=2 \\\\ 1x+1y+(-1)z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{x}$, we replace the first column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3-4)-2(-2-4)+(2-3) \\\\  & =-7+12-1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{4}{-1}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43108/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c540ac-3cb5-5e0e-9b7b-5e2ccf1615c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43108"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73697/selection/40a1a273986776af283f3fe5271d8cce9b3f9fa9c2c7fc5bf8516dd5a30de4b0" :answer/id #uuid "f2c718e2-085f-5236-a6ab-d43af7fd4e51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73697/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae" :answer/id #uuid "67c4592e-e8f1-5fff-a8e7-04ec76a80bac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73697/selection/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" :answer/id #uuid "9aea1b29-1052-5eb9-92e2-6402ad2c3839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73697/selection/e3dbb6296906b72dd0511b45b9171b9cca162c2f0d1c5924ef315cf1c16044f5" :answer/id #uuid "dece14b5-eabd-54c7-815b-02f667dfc802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73697/selection/99308c630bb61642567370331cf7f00923f341daf010971193b3aeace8b32c69" :answer/id #uuid "7e75b2d4-2ec6-546a-9163-18372f5726e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73697/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a573acf5-5d18-5677-96ba-a9902cea3820" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73697/selection/99308c630bb61642567370331cf7f00923f341daf010971193b3aeace8b32c69" :answer-field/choices ["q-73697/selection/40a1a273986776af283f3fe5271d8cce9b3f9fa9c2c7fc5bf8516dd5a30de4b0" "q-73697/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae" "q-73697/selection/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" "q-73697/selection/e3dbb6296906b72dd0511b45b9171b9cca162c2f0d1c5924ef315cf1c16044f5" "q-73697/selection/99308c630bb61642567370331cf7f00923f341daf010971193b3aeace8b32c69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73697" :question/id #uuid "3eb0f84f-ed93-5ec9-9f41-7e345c8100c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-73697" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+5z=-1 \\\\ 2x+3y+2z=0 \\\\ x+4y=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $x=-4$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $15,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x}=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ k & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ k & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-8)+(0-2k)+5(0-3k) \\\\  & =8-2k-15k \\\\  & =8-17k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D}=\\frac{8-17k}{15}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $x=-4.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8-17k}{15} & =-4 \\\\ 8-17k & =-60 \\\\ -17k & =-68 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73697/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7263e25b-117e-528c-b2ad-2624f325da35"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73697"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-139989/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "900594ef-620f-5515-ab8e-9c274ec25137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139989/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "fefd5d19-100b-5664-81cc-26501355674f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139989/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "c85a3b82-38e5-54e3-a8f7-5d5ed5ba2359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139989/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "de78559d-341b-5488-961d-a0f323e6ae69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139989/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "048b571e-6bf6-5d73-b7f8-73b5053faeab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139989/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7df0c7-70bc-577a-9397-7a95562c6a2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-139989/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-139989/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-139989/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" "q-139989/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" "q-139989/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-139989/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-139989" :question/id #uuid "7cfc346f-1d04-59ed-8cd5-10d007bfbb4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-139989" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y-2z=-7 \\\\ 2x+y-4z=-10 \\\\ 3x-3y-2z=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $16,$ then $z=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system to reveal the coefficients:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+(-5)y+(-2z)=-7 \\\\ 2x+1y+(-4)z=-10 \\\\ 3x+(-3)y+(-2)z=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing the determinant of the coefficients matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find ${D}_{z}$, we replace the third column by the right-hand side of the system, and calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{z}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ -3 & -7\\end{aligned}|-(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{aligned}|+(-7)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-7-30)+5(-14+30)-7(-6-3) \\\\  & =-111+80+63 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying Cramer's rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{{D}_{z}}{D}=\\frac{32}{16}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-139989/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c540ac-3cb5-5e0e-9b7b-5e2ccf1615c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139989"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140042/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" :answer/id #uuid "8775507c-d68a-5979-b602-569e465ad862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140042/selection/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" :answer/id #uuid "678660cc-9c2f-50f5-ad0d-b1ad439ffc41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140042/selection/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" :answer/id #uuid "89297b27-f64d-5d33-b5ba-ba8b48f2abf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140042/selection/f9a36dc20554097250ff0324e179977bb892219ae9b27b5c2ca8864aac6c0450" :answer/id #uuid "cca2f1d7-a505-59f8-ba3d-bad1763a552e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140042/selection/e3dbb6296906b72dd0511b45b9171b9cca162c2f0d1c5924ef315cf1c16044f5" :answer/id #uuid "f9a291f1-8422-5b9a-a0eb-11bfcca1983a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140042/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b90e78f8-d525-5131-8c50-118e29fcbf1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140042/selection/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" :answer-field/choices ["q-140042/selection/d8632041aa9cb2a71b6ada1b8f9b15e5f58f906bc98b3276e25ff9a0f4ed73ae" "q-140042/selection/fec406b037c336df04ddc47abb8cf02e3ae194404415f3659041d4a99c636727" "q-140042/selection/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" "q-140042/selection/f9a36dc20554097250ff0324e179977bb892219ae9b27b5c2ca8864aac6c0450" "q-140042/selection/e3dbb6296906b72dd0511b45b9171b9cca162c2f0d1c5924ef315cf1c16044f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140042" :question/id #uuid "cb48b856-28da-5ef9-a5c0-dcc3cc94f523" :question/math-academy-id "q-140042" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ be the unique solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y-5z=1 \\\\ 2x+3y-3z=k \\\\ -5x+3y+7z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $y=-1$ and that the determinant of the coefficient matrix is equal to $-19,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the determinant of the coefficients matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D=|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|=-19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y}=|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -3 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}| & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & -3 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}|+(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(7k-6)-(14-15)-5(-4+5k) \\\\  & =21k-18+1+20-25k \\\\  & =-4k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{-4k+3}{-19}.\n$$\n\nFrom the problem statement, we know that $y=-1.$ So, we can solve for $k$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4k+3}{-19} & =-1 \\\\ -4k+3 & =19 \\\\ -4k & =16 \\\\ k & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-140042/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7263e25b-117e-528c-b2ad-2624f325da35"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
